# New session row

This scenario creates several repo-backed picker entries, with both live tmux
sessions and discoverable repos that do not have live sessions. It verifies that
the ephemeral new-session row is selectable when the query is non-empty, with
names disambiguated from live sessions as needed.

    :bins jj cat

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', and 'cat' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ jj describe -R alpha -m "alpha commit" (exit: 0)
    :$ jj git init beta (exit: 0)
    :$ jj describe -R beta -m "beta commit" (exit: 0)
    :$ jj git init gamma (exit: 0)
    :$ jj describe -R gamma -m "gamma commit" (exit: 0)
    :$ jj git init delta (exit: 0)
    :$ jj describe -R delta -m "delta commit" (exit: 0)

Launch live sessions for `alpha` and `gamma`, while `beta` and `delta` remain
repo-only entries discovered through the CLI globs.

    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -t alpha @smth.repo alpha (success)
    :t new-session -d -s gamma "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -t gamma @smth.repo gamma (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r 'alpha' -r 'beta' -r 'gamma' -r 'delta'" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :pane ui:0.0
    :settle (settled)

Initially the query is empty, so no new-session candidate is available.
Pressing `C-n` should do nothing and leave the picker open in the same state.

    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session:
  8/8 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
 ⬤ ui                                                                                                                  ┃
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────







```

    :k C-n
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session:
  8/8 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
 ⬤ ui                                                                                                                  ┃
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────







```

Typing a prefix of the live `alpha` session makes the new-session row selectable,
because `alp` is not an exact live session name.

    :k alp M-up
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: alp
  2/8 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  alp                                                                                                                 ┃
 ⬤ alpha                                    alpha                                                                      │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────







```

Completing the live session name causes the new-session row's name to become
disambiguated.

    :k ha
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: alpha
  2/8 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  alpha~1                                                                                                             ┃
 ⬤ alpha                                    alpha                                                                      │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────







```

Completing the name of the non-live `beta` repo removes the disambiguation from
the new-session row, because there is no live session named `beta`.

    :k C-u beta
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: beta
  1/8 | [C-r] repo: none
   beta                                                                                                                ┃
▌  beta                                     ~/beta                                                                     ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) beta commit
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh




```

